    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0136" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg18"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pitkin to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Buenos Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 20, 1889</date>.
                        (Received December 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Minister Hanna’s No. 235, May
                    20, 1889, reciting certain embarrassments to citizens of the United States
                    contemplating marriage here and inclosing translation of the civil marriage law
                    of this country of November 12, 1888, I have the honor to invite your attention
                    to a new enactment herewith inclosed on the subject-matter, involving certain
                    repeals and amendments whereby it will be seen that a certificate <pb
                        facs="0137" n="19" xml:id="pg19"/> of birth or baptism, and in case of
                    previous marriage a certificate of death, are no longer required and that a
                    certificate of civil status is likewise dispensed with.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John R. G.
                    Pitkin.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d9-a1.xml" xpointer="d9-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
